<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Information technology Pre-Board</title>
<style>
body { font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.4; margin: 20px; }
.header { text-align: center; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; padding-bottom: 10px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class='header'>
    <h2>RRB Group of Schools</h2>
    <h3>Pre-Board — Information technology (Class 9 A)</h3>
</div>
<table width='100%' style='margin-bottom:15px;font-weight:bold;'>
    <tr>
        <td>Time Allowed: 3 Hours</td>
        <td align='right'>Maximum Marks: 70</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Teacher: GAURAV SHUKLA</td>
        <td align='right'>Date: 20/08/2026</td>
    </tr>
</table>
<hr>
<h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Choose the correct answer for each of the following questions.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Which of the following is an example of non-verbal communication?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Written letter</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Facial expressions</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Spoken speech</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Telephone conversation</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Which keyboard shortcut is used to cut selected text in LibreOffice Writer?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Ctrl + C</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Ctrl + V</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Ctrl + X</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Ctrl + Z</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> In LibreOffice Writer, which menu is used to insert a table into the document?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) File</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Edit</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Table</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Format</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> By default, numbers entered into an electronic spreadsheet cell are aligned to the:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Left</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Right</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Center</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Justified</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> Which function in a spreadsheet is used to find the maximum value in a range of cells?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) HIGH()</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) MAX()</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) MAXIMUM()</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) LARGE()</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q6.</strong> Which view in presentation software is best suited for reordering slides easily?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Normal View</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Slide Sorter View</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Notes Page View</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Outline View</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q7.</strong> ITeS stands for:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Information Technology Enabled Services</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) International Technology Extended Systems</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Information Telecommunication Enterprise Services</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Integrated Technology Enabled Solutions</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q8.</strong> While using touch typing technique, which finger rests on the key 'F' on a standard QWERTY keyboard?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Left Index Finger</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Right Index Finger</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Left Thumb</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Right Middle Finger</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q9.</strong> Which of the following is considered a non-renewable energy resource?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Solar Energy</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Wind Energy</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Coal</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Hydroelectric Energy</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q10.</strong> An individual who sets up a business, taking on financial risks in the hope of profit, is known as a/an:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Employee</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Manager</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Entrepreneur</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Operator</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section B: Assertion-Reason Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Select the correct option from (a), (b), (c), and (d) for each question.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q11.</strong> Assertion (A): Home row keys are the primary row where fingers rest while typing.
Reason (R): The keys 'A, S, D, F' and 'J, K, L, ;' form the Home Row on a standard QWERTY keyboard.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q12.</strong> Assertion (A): Absolute cell referencing in spreadsheets does not change when copied to another cell.
Reason (R): Absolute referencing uses the '' sign before the column letter and row number.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q13.</strong> Assertion (A): Verbal communication includes both oral and written forms.
Reason (R): Written communication uses symbols, gestures, and body movements.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q14.</strong> Assertion (A): Goal setting is an important aspect of self-management.
Reason (R): Setting SMART goals helps individuals stay focused and track their performance effectively.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q15.</strong> Assertion (A): BPO enables companies to outsource non-core business operational tasks.
Reason (R): IT-BPM sector contributes significantly to India's GDP and employment growth.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q16.</strong> Assertion (A): LibreOffice Impress saves files with the extension .odp by default.
Reason (R): .docx is the default file format for LibreOffice Impress presentations.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q17.</strong> Assertion (A): Self-motivation helps individuals perform tasks independently without external pressure.
Reason (R): Self-motivated people lack self-confidence and directional clarity.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q18.</strong> Assertion (A): Headers appear at the top margin and Footers appear at the bottom margin of pages.
Reason (R): Headers and Footers can be set to repeat automatically on all pages of a document.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q19.</strong> Assertion (A): Green Skills promote economic development without harming the environment.
Reason (R): Over-exploitation of natural resources is a key principle of sustainable green skills.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q20.</strong> Assertion (A): Slide transition defines the visual effect that occurs when moving from one slide to another during a show.
Reason (R): Custom animation controls how specific elements on a single slide appear, emphasis, or exit.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section C: Very Short Answer Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions briefly.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q21.</strong> Distinguish between Data and Information with suitable examples for each.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q22.</strong> Define 'Touch Typing'. Mention any two ergonomic rules for correct typing posture.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q23.</strong> Differentiate between Relative Cell Referencing and Absolute Cell Referencing in spreadsheets.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q24.</strong> What is a Watermark in a word processor? Mention its primary purpose.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q25.</strong> State any two key benefits of using electronic spreadsheets over manual record keeping.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q26.</strong> Define Business Process Outsourcing (BPO). Give two examples of services offered by BPO companies.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q27.</strong> What is effective communication? Mention any two common barriers to effective communication.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q28.</strong> Differentiate between Slide Transition and Custom Animation in presentation software.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q29.</strong> Define Self-Management. Name two important self-management skills required by students.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q30.</strong> What is meant by Sustainable Development? Mention one eco-friendly habit.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section D: Short Answer Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions in detail.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q31.</strong> Effective communication relies on principles known as the 7 Cs. List and explain any three of them.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q32.</strong> Define the following spreadsheet terminology:
(a) Active Cell
(b) Cell Range
(c) Formula Bar</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q33.</strong> What is Mail Merge in Digital Documentation? Explain the role of the Main Document and Data Source in this feature.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q34.</strong> Explain how Information Technology (IT) plays a critical role in the following fields:
(a) Healthcare
(b) Education
(c) Banking</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q35.</strong> What is Entrepreneurship? Describe any two important qualities or characteristics of a successful entrepreneur.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section E: Long Answer Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions in detail with clear explanations.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q36.</strong> Answer the sub-questions based on spreadsheet operations and functions:</div><ol style='padding-left:20px;margin-top:4px;'><li>Write the spreadsheet formula to calculate the total sum of marks stored in cells B2 to F2.</li><li>Write the function to find the average of the same cell range (B2:F2).</li><li>Explain how Conditional Formatting can be used to highlight marks below 40 in red.</li><li>Explain the step-by-step process to freeze the top row containing table headers.</li><li>Differentiate between the COUNT() and COUNTA() functions in a spreadsheet.</li></ol><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q37.</strong> Answer the following multi-part questions regarding Digital Documentation:</div><ol style='padding-left:20px;margin-top:4px;'><li>What is Page Formatting? Explain any four formatting features available under Page Setup (e.g., Margins, Orientation, Page Size, Columns).</li><li>Describe the steps required to insert an image into a document and apply text wrapping around it.</li></ol><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q38.</strong> Answer the following multi-part questions regarding Presentation Software and Employability Skills:</div><ol style='padding-left:20px;margin-top:4px;'><li>Explain the steps involved in creating a new presentation using a built-in presentation template.</li><li>Discuss five essential guidelines that should be followed to design an effective and appealing visual presentation.</li></ol>
</body>
</html>